      <marc:subfield code="a">An elderly couple was brutally murdered. All the evidence pointed to Akira Kiobara as the killer. However, due to a car accident, he conveniently lost all memory of the hours before and after the crime…With time running out before Kiobara’s execution, execution officer Nango teams up with Junichi—a man recently released on parole—to investigate the case, hoping to clear the name of the death row inmate who now remembers nothing. But the only clue they uncover is Kiobara’s vague recollection of “walking on some steps.” The execution date draws near, yet the case remains shrouded in mystery. The only lead—the &quot;steps&quot;—seems to have vanished into thin air…</marc:subfield>
